JOINS:
JOINS are used to combine data from one or more tables based on a related column between them.

Types:
(1) Inner join: It return all the matching rows from both the tables.

(2) Left join: It returns all the data from left table and only matching data from
right table.

(3) Right Join: It returns all the data from right table and only matching data
from left table.

(4) Full outer join: Return all the data from both the tables whether they 
matched or not.

(5) Cross join: Returns the cartesian product of two tables.

(6) Self join: Join a table with itself. commonly used for hierarchical data such as 
Employee-Manager reltionship.

